{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe `trust_but_verify::domain::Domain` trait includes a method for obtaining a node's\nsuccessors with a given label:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Return the target node identities for this source and label.\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        source_node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires `Domain::outgoing_edges(&self, source_node, label) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>`. It must return the target node identities for that source and label.\n\nCoverage by obligation:\n- **Signature and trait member.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` implements `Domain` for `Relationships`. It calls `outgoing_edges` through the generic helper `successors<G: Domain>`, so it compiles against the required signature, including the `Result<Vec<NodeId>, Error>` return type.\n- **Targets for source and label.**\n  - The contracts test asserts that `(1, Label(2))` returns `[3, 2, 3]`. This also shows that order and duplicates are kept.\n  - It asserts that `(1, Label(3))` returns `[4]`. Together with the previous case, this shows the label selects the result.\n  - It asserts that `(1, Label(4))` and `(2, Label(2))` return empty vectors. These are the no-edge cases for an unmatched label and an unmatched source.\n- **Error outcome.** The same test calls `outgoing_edges` on `Identity(255)`. It asserts the `Err` carries `255` and can be sent.\n- **Real domain behavior.** `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[test_edges_select_only_tests_for_the_requested_requirement]` calls `outgoing_edges` on `HabeasDomain`.\n  - With the `Tests` label, it asserts that exactly the test source for the requested requirement is returned. The unrelated test is excluded.\n  - With the `Implements` label, it asserts the result differs from the `Tests` result.\n  - It asserts that a source node with no `Tests` edges returns an empty vector.\n- **Validation context.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents]` exercises edge retrieval through `ValidationContext`. It checks label filtering, duplicate retention, empty results, and error propagation (`Err(\"edges\")`).\n\nThe `{test}` marker on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[nested_label_schema_references_resolve_from_the_tool_parameters_root]` is only tangentially related, because that test checks a JSON schema. It adds nothing to the coverage above, and the other tests already cover every obligation.\n\nI found no obligation without a test and no assertion that contradicts the requirement.",
